 "statement": "Annotated blind from the Beinecke scan only: canvas 1006196 ('68r', a foldout of three panels); f68r1 is the leftmost panel (canvas x about 280-2530), whose structure fits the line ids (paragraph lines at the top, 29 star labels f68r1.8-.36, one circular text f68r1.37). Drawn: 29 eight-pointed (some seven-pointed) stars with a tan/yellow wash scattered over the panel, each with one short word beside it (to its right, except one with the word to its left); seven have a small open circle at the centre and two a dark dot; one at the upper left is drawn faintly in grey. A sun-like circle with a frontal face and braided hair, ringed by about 24 small curved rays, sits under the top paragraph with words inside the circle; a crescent with a blue inner ring and a face sits at the bottom inside a ring of text. A long thin arc runs down the right side. A pale blue-green radiating shape behind the middle stars looks like show-through from the other side of the leaf and is not annotated. No star label line id is assigned to a star: the line ids carry no position and the blind rule forbids reading the words. Each star carries its position as fractions of the panel (x right, y down) and its rank in row-by-row reading order, so a position map of the label lines can join them later. The 29 stars equal the 29 star label lines.",
